WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.120
In John's Gospel, Jesus prays
that his followers may all be one.

2
00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:09.130
Yet Christians split:
East and West in 1054,

3
00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:11.350
then again at the Reformation.

4
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:15.510
In 1948, churches founded the
World Council of Churches:

5
00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:17.380
a fellowship of churches.

6
00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:20.000
But the Catholic Church is not a member.

7
00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:22.860
So can Christians be one again?

8
00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:25.200
And what would one even mean?

9
00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:30.230
In this mission, you'll see why Jesus'
prayer drives the search for unity.

10
00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:33.260
Then you'll see how churches
view one another today,

11
00:00:33.310 --> 00:00:35.370
and how close they have come.

12
00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:39.010
Your mission: find out what
Christian unity could mean,

13
00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:40.990
and how close churches have come.
